From a6f184c592d37b2c78211e2652591e36f3b73534 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: snap-pea <snap-pea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 02:04:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/19] opencl: faster q8_0 speculative-verify GEMVs (small-M
 split-K, lm_head local-memory activations)

Verify batches (2..8 columns) on Qwen3.6-35B-A3B:
- small-M dense weights (M <= 2048: shared-expert gate/up/down, K/V) went to the
  cooperative-K GEMM, which tiles 4 rows per lane into 64-lane work-groups: M = 512
  is two work-groups on the 16-CU X2-90. New kernel_gemv_noshuffle_q8_0_q8a_dp4a_mc_splitk:
  int8 activations, weights read once for all columns, K split over up to 8 slices
  (at least two blocks per slice), summed by kernel_gemv_splitk_reduce_f32.
  512x2048 n=5: 45.4 -> 15.8 us; 2048x512 n=5: 17.2 -> 15.5 us.
  Opt out: GGML_OPENCL_Q8_NS_MC_SPLITK=0, slices: GGML_OPENCL_Q8_NS_MC_KSPLIT.
- the multi-column dp4a GEMV (lm_head 248320x2048) re-read all columns' activations
  per subgroup; kernel_mul_mv_q8_0_q8a_dp4a_mc_lds stages them in local memory once
  per 8-subgroup work-group (ncol*K <= 16 KB). n=5: 8689 -> 7893 us.
  Subgroups: GGML_OPENCL_Q8_MC_LDS_NSG (0 = old kernel). Column loops unrolled.

pp5 @ d512: 73.0 -> 76.4 t/s. Agent-prompt MTP bench (temp 0.6, 4 prompts x 2 seeds,
2 reps): 39.6 -> 40.9 tok/s. test-backend-ops MUL_MAT 1690/1690. Adds q6_K MUL_MAT_ID
2..8-token eval cases and Qwen3.6 verify-shape MUL_MAT perf cases.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
